---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy">
  <div class="screen">
    <div class="page-head reveal">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">legal</div>
        <h1>Privacy policy<span class="cursor"></span></h1>
        <p>Last updated 5 November 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="legal grow scroll">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your Google name and email address, used to sign you in.</li>
        <li>A Google access token for read-only Gmail access, encrypted at rest.</li>
        <li>Plugins you create, and which plugins you turn on.</li>
        <li>Answers to plugin questions about your new emails, plus short matched snippets for plugins that use rules.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not keep</h2>
      <p>
        Emails are read on our servers, answered by our own model and dropped. We never store email bodies or
        headers, and never send your emails to third-party AI services. Logs hold ids, not email content.
      </p>

      <h2>Who sees your data</h2>
      <p>
        Only plugins you turn on receive answers, and only for mail that arrives while they are on. A plugin's
        developer can fetch those answers with its API key. We do not sell your data or use it for ads.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Answers are deleted 30 days after they are fetched or after you turn the plugin off, and after 100 days
        at most. Deleting your account removes your account, token, plugins and answers.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Turn any plugin off on <a href="/subscriptions">your subscriptions page</a>.</li>
        <li>Delete your account from the same page.</li>
        <li>Revoke access at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google account permissions</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google user data</h2>
      <p>
        Iris's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>We use only the cookies needed to keep you signed in and protect forms. No tracking or analytics.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We will update this page and its date when this policy changes.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
